    `Father, I receive the call to perfection today — not as a crushing standard that produces despair but as the most generous invitation available. You are calling me to fullness, to maturity, to the complete development of everything You placed in me before I was born. Be perfect as your heavenly Father is perfect is not a rebuke. It is a vision. It is the declaration of what You intend to make me if I cooperate with the work You have already begun. Let prayer, holiness, and the pursuit of Christlikeness be the lifestyle of my ordinary days — not events I attend or peaks I occasionally reach, but the consistent, daily, undramatic texture of a life that is always oriented toward You. Rejoicing. Praying. Giving thanks. In all circumstances. Not because I have achieved a spiritual state where all circumstances feel good, but because I have found in You something that is better than the circumstances — and the finding of it has permanently reoriented the way I move through the world. Do not let me settle for good enough. Keep the vision of teleios before me — the full maturity, the complete formation, the full ripening of everything You are growing in me.`
